  "notes": "Made by an AI agent (Claude Opus, Anthropic) in the maintainers' newcomer study on 2026-11-05, as a new design rather than a variation of a shipped one; the agent chose the player name. The design is a carry-select adder with 6-bit blocks, for every N >= 1: Q = N/6 blocks and an R = N%6 ripple tail, both integer localparams. Block j keeps two ripple chains in row j of the 2-D arrays c0 (block carry-in 0) and c1 (block carry-in 1); a multiplexer row cs picks the carry into each bit by the block carry cb[j], the block carries ripple through one multiplexer per block, and the sum bits are p ^ carry, written in two trailing loops. The block size and the placement of the sum assigns were chosen by sweeps scored with score/ppa.py. The proof takes the sv_structure / sv_interface / sv_equations / sv_bridge / sv_cover route with its own rank function over the site ids; its arithmetic is plain Lean, generic in the block size (a ripple carry restarted at any position, two chain lemmas and a multiplexer lemma), and shows that the selected carries are the ripple carries, so the design meets CombLib.AddView and add_spec finishes the proof. The comments in both files are the agent's. Proof ported by the maintainers for the 2026-11-06 range change; design unchanged.",
